ActualOutput_Q4:
The annual monitoring report on vessels registered on the South African Ship Register developed as targeted. 

The report indicates that, currently, there are twelve (12) merchant vessels registered under the South African flag as follows:

•	Four bulk carriers from Vuka marine;
•	Three (03) Linsen Nambi Bunker Burgees;
•	Three (03) from AMSOL Oil Tanker Siqalo
•	Firefighter vessel Siqalo;
•	Nomasa offshore supply vessel;
•	A marine crew services vessel named Viewer Harriet; and
•	Meneva-owned vessel Antel.

Furthermore, SAMSA is in engagement with Nduna Marine to register the Bow Cecil under the South African flag.

ActualOutput_Q2:
Further stakeholder consultations on the updated Public Transport Funding Model were conducted.

The purpose of the consultations was to provide progress with regards to the development of the Public Transport Funding Model and Public Transport Subsidy Policy.

The following resolutions were taken.

•	NDoT to organise a two (2) days’ workshop to deal with the implementation of the MINMEC resolutions;

•	Discuss the appointment of the task team as per the MINMEC resolutions;
•	Discuss the terms of reference relating to the review of the escalation formula;
•	NDoT to distribute the Public Transport Funding Model document and Presentation to provinces for inputs and comments; and

•	Provinces to ensure that signed PTOG monthly and quarterly reports are submitted on time.

